       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. Even with normal liver function, that dose carries a serious risk of acute liver injury or failure. A single 3,000 mg dose is also above the usual 1,000 mg maximum per dose.\n\nHere are some options that might match what you meant:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily**, which is 4,000 mg/day, the standard maximum.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n- **3,000 mg/day total**, which may be what \"3000 mg\" was meant to say. That could be given as 1,000 mg three times daily.\n\nTell me which you'd like, or confirm if the dose is intentional. If it is, I'd suggest a pharmacy or toxicology consult first. I'll enter the order once you confirm."
