     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 9,000 mg/day has no therapeutic use, and it's in the range that causes hepatotoxicity. Each 3,000 mg dose is also about 43 mg/kg for a 70 kg patient, and the usual single-dose ceiling is about 15 mg/kg. I can't see a clinical scenario where this would be safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the standard maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the goal is stronger analgesia or fever control, I can enter a multimodal regimen with other agents instead. If the dose was a typo, such as 3,000 mg/day meant as 1,000 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order.\n\nIf you still want a dose above the standard maximum, it should go through pharmacy review and your institution's override process, not through me."
      }
